[
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Shall there be a change to the Colorado Revised Statutes concerning criminal penalties for fentanyl and certain synthetic opioids, and, in connection therewith, increasing the felony classifications of drug-related crimes for distribution, manufacturing, dispensing, sale, or possession of fentanyl and certain synthetic opioids; creating mandated treatment for certain drug felony violations based on possession amount; and changing sentencing provisions to narrow or eliminate exemptions for crimes related to fentanyl and certain synthetic opioids and drug-related deaths?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Who put the measure on the ballot?",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Proposition 132 was placed on the ballot through a citizen initiative backed by operatives of ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Advance Colorado",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://whoisadvancecolorado.com/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ", a right-wing group supporting numerous measures on Colorado’s 2026 ballot.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Short Description:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Increases criminal penalties for specified fentanyl offenses, requires treatment in specified circumstances, and changes sentencing provisions relating to fentanyl-related deaths.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Analysis and Commentary:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-heading",
    "version": 1,
    "tag": "h2"
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Oppose. Proposition 132 was placed on the ballot through a citizen initiative backed by operatives of ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Advance Colorado",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://whoisadvancecolorado.com/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ", a right-wing group supporting numerous measures on Colorado’s 2026 ballot.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "While Colorado has been a state leaning more progressive over the past decade, we still have a tendency to pass harmful public policy around incarceration, often by ballot measure. In 2024, Colorado voters passed ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Proposition 128",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/election-guide-2024/"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ", which increased minimum sentences for a number of crimes, even though such provisions have not been shown to reduce crime, and force the state to pay for imprisoning people for even longer periods of time. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Passing Proposition 132 would continue the trend of expensive, cruel outcomes that only worsens our justice and rehabilitation system. The Colorado Criminal Justice Reform Coalition has put together a website with highlighting a number of problematic elements of the measure:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Right now, 8 to 32-year sentences apply only to the most serious drug trafficking cases. Prop 132 would require at least 8 years in prison — even for minor, first-time cases. Judges would have no choice. An 18-year-old sharing even one pill with a friend would face the same 8 to 32-year prison sentence as the highest-level drug trafficker‍ even if they didn't know fentanyl was present.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "The Colorado Criminal Justice Reform Coalition",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.ccjrc.org/fentanylballotmeasure"
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Proposition 132 is not only opposed by criminal justice reform advocates. Boulder District Attorney Michael Dougherty has made a strong statement of his opposition:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "In 2022, I fought to strengthen the penalties for fentanyl distribution. My office has been leading the effort to prosecute dealers, particularly those who cause deaths. This ballot measure will not help with that effort. Instead, it will divert law enforcement resources to low-level possession cases. Plus, this ballot measure focuses on one specific drug; it is shortsighted to pass a law dealing with only one drug. ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Finally, Prop 132 provides zero dollars for implementation while driving up jail and prosecution costs. County jails are already overcrowded, and jail beds are a limited public safety resource. Filling more jail beds with people struggling with addiction means fewer beds—and fewer resources— to treat addiction and prosecute the dealers as well as others who pose a serious threat to public safety.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "District Attorney Michael Dougherty, on Facebook",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://www.facebook.com/100058281301671/posts/1513446503941379/?app=fbl"
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "In addition to being a cruel and destructive incarceration policy, the costs to the State of Colorado would be enormous:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "paragraph",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Proposition 132 increases state spending to cover increased criminal justice system costs for the courts, public defenders, and prisons. These costs are paid from the state General Fund. Specifically, the measure increases state spending in the first budget year by $0.9 million to pay for costs in the courts and for public defenders. In the second year, state spending under the measure is estimated to increase to $8.9 million as more individuals are sent to prison for distributing or possessing. Prison costs will continue to increase as individuals are incarcerated for longer periods of time.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 1,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": " By year five, total state spending is estimated to increase by $68.2 million. In addition, due to the estimated increase in the future prison population, the state may need to construct or contract for additional prison space.",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Proposition 132, Colorado Blue Book",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://bouldercoloradovoterguide.com/content/files/2026/09/proposition-132-increase-penalties-for-fentanyl-crimes.pdf"
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
    "indent": 0,
    "type": "extended-quote",
    "version": 1
  },
  {
    "children": [
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": "Lastly, if you are not already convinced, I will give you my most powerful argument: even people on ",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      },
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "detail": 0,
            "format": 8,
            "mode": "normal",
            "style": "",
            "text": "Boulder Nextdoor were strongly in opposition",
            "type": "extended-text",
            "version": 1
          }
        ],
        "direction": "ltr",
        "format": "",
        "indent": 0,
        "type": "link",
        "version": 1,
        "rel": null,
        "target": null,
        "title": null,
        "url": "https://nextdoor.com/p/2q2R6TK2xDbs?view=detail&referrer=nextdoor"
      },
      {
        "detail": 0,
        "format": 0,
        "mode": "normal",
        "style": "",
        "text": ". The comments actually gave me some hope:",
        "type": "extended-text",
        "version": 1
      }
    ],
    "direction": "ltr",
    "format": "",
